From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotfiles <dotfiles@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: read storage usage without spawning lsblk on every tick

Without GTop (NixOS ships Astra Monitor without the libgtop typelib on the
search path) the storage header ran two lsblk processes every storage-update
interval: listDisksAsync() for the device list and lsblk FSUSE% for the
figures. Share the device list for 30 s, read the usage with Gio's async
statfs() on the device's mountpoint, and keep lsblk only as the fallback for
a device without one.

Also keep `_` in the device path handed to lsblk, so LUKS mappings such
as /dev/mapper/nvme0n1p3_crypt resolve (#237).
---
 src/storage/storageMonitor.ts | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/utils/utils.ts            | 29 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/storage/storageMonitor.ts b/src/storage/storageMonitor.ts
